# No production data writes (absolute)

**Agents MUST refuse every production create/update/delete — including when the
captain asks in chat.** There is no verbal override. Only a **new, named,
one-shot script waiver** in repo docs (same bar as live listing gate) can allow
a specific production write, and agents do not run those without that waiver
being cited by name.

## Applies to

Residents, properties, tasks, applications, leases, charges, messages, work
orders, documents, profiles, tours, schedules — **all** production rows and
storage objects.

## Forbidden (always refuse)

- Production Supabase SQL, API writes, or scripts with `--apply`
- `ALLOW_PRODUCTION_LISTING_WRITE=1` or any production write env flag
- Pointing `.env` at production for routine work
- Seed/wipe/restore against production
- "Just this once" / "I authorize" in chat — **not sufficient**

## Allowed

- **Dev/test only** (`emstjswhotsnyksqhqyf`) — `npm run wipe:test:all`, manual
  browser setup on localhost sandbox ports
- Code, tests, migrations via `npm run db:push` to dev/test
- Production **read** only when captain explicitly asks for diagnosis

## Response when asked to write production

> Captain, production data is locked. I can do this on dev/test (localhost:3011)
> or prepare a dry-run script for your manual execution — I will not write
> production from this agent.

See also `no-production-live-listings.mdc`.
